From b2bec2e97bc2e49a66b79b31b57c9ef508253572 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashesh Vidyut <asheshvidyut@google.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 02:18:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Bound and retry the xds interop server startup probe

The server's port is reserved, released, then bound by the server
subprocess; in that window another process can take the port (even as
the ephemeral source port of an unrelated loopback connection), the
server then fails to start, and the wait_for_ready probe blocked
forever, timing the test out with no diagnostics (confirmed by an absl
SIGTERM stack dump showing the main thread parked in
grpc_completion_queue_next). Give the probe a deadline, retry once
with a fresh port, and dump the server's output when it never becomes
ready.
---
 .../interop/xds_interop_client_test.py        | 122 +++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 78 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/python/grpcio_tests/tests_py3_only/interop/xds_interop_client_test.py b/src/python/grpcio_tests/tests_py3_only/interop/xds_interop_client_test.py
